-From bec62b9807378076b8c04b49051cedf5d9442778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Aaron Guise <aaron@guise.net.nz>
-Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2025 11:26:12 +1200
-Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix CardDAV sync-collection compatibility with eM Client
- and similar clients
-
-Some CardDAV clients like eM Client send sync-collection requests with Depth::Zero
-but expect them to be processed as Depth::One to include child resources.
-
-This changes the default depth handling for sync-collection from 0 to 1 to match
-client expectations while preserving the explicit Depth::One and Depth::Infinity
-behavior.
-
-Also adds a test case that verifies sync-collection works correctly with the
-getetag + getcontenttype property combination that eM Client uses, ensuring
-contacts are returned with their etags for proper synchronization.
